# Copy to `.env.local` to run analytics against a real project. Without it the
# site builds and runs exactly as before, minus PostHog — which is what a local
# checkout should do, so development never writes into the production project.

# The PostHog project's public key. It ships inside the JS bundle and is meant
# to be readable by anyone, so this is not a secret; ingestion is authorised by
# the project's allowed origins, not by this string. Set it in Vercel for both
# Production and Preview — NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build time, so changing
# it needs a redeploy, not just a restart.
#
# PostHog → Settings → Project → Project API key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_000000000000000000000000000000000000000000
